.\" Manual page for forge.
.TH FORGE 1 "2026-08-24" "forge 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
forge \- graphical and command-line package manager frontend for Arch Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forge
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B forge search
.I QUERY
.br
.B forge info
.I PACKAGE
.br
.B forge install
.RI [ \-\-reviewed ]
.I PACKAGE...
.br
.B forge remove
.I PACKAGE...
.br
.B forge update
.RI [ \-y ]
.br
.B forge list
.RI [ \-\-source
.IR SOURCE ]
.br
.B forge config-path
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Forge
is a package-management frontend for Arch Linux and Arch-based distributions.
It orchestrates existing packaging systems through a common backend
abstraction:
.TP
.B Repositories (pacman)
Official packages. pacman itself performs all dependency resolution; Forge
never reimplements it. Privileged operations are executed via
.BR pkexec (1)
so the desktop polkit agent asks for authentication. Forge never invokes
sudo.
.TP
.B AUR
Community packages from aur.archlinux.org. Searches use the documented RPC
v5 API. Before any AUR package is built, Forge fetches its source with git,
displays the PKGBUILD for review, lists build dependencies obtained from
.B makepkg \-\-printsrcinfo
and requires explicit confirmation. Builds run unprivileged via makepkg;
only the resulting archive installation uses polkit.
.TP
.B Flatpak
Applications from Flatpak remotes, in per-user or system-wide
installations. User-scope operations never require authentication.
.PP
Running
.B forge
without a command launches the graphical interface (GTK4 / libadwaita).
Every CLI subcommand shares the same backend architecture as the GUI.
A transaction preview is always shown before any significant operation;
nothing is installed, removed or upgraded without explicit confirmation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B search
Search across enabled sources. Options:
.RS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-source " " \fISOURCE\fR
Restrict to \fBrepos\fR, \fBaur\fR or \fBflatpak\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-installed
Only show installed packages.
.RE
.TP
.B info
Show detailed metadata for one package: version, source, dependencies,
optional dependencies, homepage, licenses, maintainer, sizes and install
status.
.TP
.B install
Install one or more packages. A preview (including dependencies pulled in
by pacman, download/installed sizes and conflicts) is shown first.
Options:
.RS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Skip the confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-reviewed
AUR only: assert that you have reviewed the PKGBUILD. Required unless
disabled in the configuration file.
.RE
.TP
.B remove
Remove packages. The preview shows the exact removal set computed by pacman
itself (\fB\-Rs\fR semantics) plus which no-longer-needed dependencies would
go with them.
.TP
.B update
Refresh repository databases and apply all available updates across every
enabled backend (pacman full upgrade, AUR rebuilds, Flatpak updates).
.TP
.B list
List installed packages, optionally filtered by source.
.TP
.B config-path
Print the location of the configuration file.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration lives at
.I ~/.config/forge/config.toml
and every key has a safe default; a missing file is not an error. See
.B /usr/share/doc/forge/examples/forge-config.toml
for a fully commented example covering: confirmation behaviour, source
visibility (pacman/AUR/Flatpak), preferred repositories, the AUR build
directory and mandatory PKGBUILD review, Flatpak scope visibility, window
preferences and parallel downloads.
.SH SECURITY NOTES
.IP \(bu 3
Package names are passed to external tools as argv elements; no shell is
ever involved and input is validated before use.
.IP \(bu 3
Privilege escalation uses polkit exclusively; sudo is never invoked and
passwords are never requested by Forge itself.
.IP \(bu 3
AUR packages are community-produced and are clearly labelled as such.
Forge refuses to build an AUR package until its PKGBUILD has been reviewed.
.IP \(bu 3
The origin of every package (repository, AUR, Flatpak remote and scope) is
displayed wherever it appears.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/forge/config.toml
User configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/forge/aur/
Default directory for cloned AUR repositories and build artefacts.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/forge.desktop
Desktop entry.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on error and 130 when cancelled.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR makepkg (8),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
Full documentation: /usr/share/doc/forge/README.md
.SH BUGS
Report issues at the project's issue tracker.
